 bring your own  bottle well if that's not a party i'm  not sure what is and that the prime  minister was in attendance so you look  back at what he said and what he did and  it just doesn't add up now where are we  in terms of the blame game and also that  investigation well there is pressure on  martin reynolds tonight some people  saying this is the  prime minister's uh principal private  secretary he's one of his civil servants  who help him in his office some people  putting the blame onto him saying why  did he put this email out but one former  cabinet minister made the point to me  tonight well he does what the prime  minister asked him to do and did he do  that off his own bat or did the prime  minister somehow know  this was happening now that  investigation is running along sue gray  will  give her verdict soon but as for the  parliamentary party i have to say i  spoke to one senior conservative mp  tonight mps have been in the commons for  votes this evening saying there is a lot  of deep unhappiness in the party at the  moment and as one mp said to me at some  point this prime minister really is  going to run out of road  beth rugby live there in downing street  for us thank you well that story is  featuring tomorrow's newspapers here  then is the metro the headline downing  it street we'll have our extended press  preview and

